  "findings": [
    "Default hyperparameters: 1.6.1 first grid point kernel=rbf, C=0.001, epsilon=0.001, max_iter=500 (grid C 0.001..100, epsilon 0.001..1); v2 declares kernel=rbf, C=1.0, epsilon=0.1 (log-uniform spaces C 1e-3..100, epsilon 1e-3..1) and `max_iter=-1` as a non-tunable value. The `defaults` variant measures the effect: with C=0.001 the 1.6.1 default is close to a constant predictor. B5 decides whether to move the v2 defaults.",
    "1.6.1 caps libsvm at 500 iterations in every grid point, which stops before convergence on realistic data (ConvergenceWarning); v2 runs to convergence unless `max_iter` is set. The `capped` variant checks that an explicit cap is applied identically.",
    "End to end, the predictions only agree statistically (class statistical): SMO stops at libsvm's default tol=1e-3, its working-set selection is discontinuous in the kernel values, and the float32 features of v2 (1e-7 relative) steer it to a different, equally valid solution (different n_iter_, differences up to the solver tolerance, e.g. 2e-3 absolute for the linear kernel). The `identical` steps feed both estimators the same float64 matrix and are exact, so the algorithm and hyperparameters are the same. The `capped` variant (max_iter=500, same path) agrees to float32 precision.",
    "1.6.1 selects the `landmark_genes` list while loading the CSVs (hyperparameter `gene_list`, a missing gene raises); the v2 preset consumes the whole gene expression view (`scaledGeneExpression` without `gene_list`). The case compares a pre-selected matrix; wiring the list into the preset belongs to B5.",
    "Features agree to float32 precision (class forward): v2 holds them as float32, 1.6.1 as float64."
  ],
